comments.body:
@skye I dug into this a bit. The DLPack code is actually working fine: it correctly understands that you have an array with a non-standard layout. It correctly builds a `PjRtBuffer` with this layout. However as soon as you wrap the buffer in an IFRT Array we have lost the game (https://github.com/openxla/xla/blob/bf3f45750f1525b7ba5f3f7b2a121817dd4ed2dd/xla/python/dlpack.cc#L493) because IFRT arrays have no way to even report that they have a non-standard layout (https://github.com/openxla/xla/blob/bf3f45750f1525b7ba5f3f7b2a121817dd4ed2dd/xla/python/ifrt/array.h#L69). Happily I think you're looking into adding that kind of support.

Note this particular example seems to only repro with `JAX_ENABLE_X64=0`, for some reason.

If adding more comprehensive layout support is far off, then I'd report an error if we see a non-standard layout in the dlpack code for now.

